  "solution": {
    "text": "<p>A trans alkene can be converted to a vicinal dihalide through a halogenation reaction. The vicinal dihalide can undergo double elimination to afford an alkyne. The alkyne can undergo partial reduction to give a cis alkene.</p><p>The reagents needed to convert&nbsp;trans<i><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>(</mo><mi>Ph</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>-</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>CH</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>=</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>CH</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>-</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><msub><mi>CH</mi><mn>3</mn></msub><mo>)</mo></math></i>&nbsp;to&nbsp;cis-<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>(</mo><mi>Ph</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>-</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>CH</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>=</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>CH</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>-</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><msub><mi>CH</mi><mn>3</mn></msub><mo>)</mo></math>&nbsp;are shown in the reaction scheme below.</p><p><img src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/pyq/jee_main/f915bf6b-e308-4d86-ad84-ed0ebbb3f799-9896079.png\" style=\"width: 600px; height: 431px;\" /></p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>&nbsp;</p>",
